# Commit as the work becomes reviewable

- Commit each finished action when it has one clear reason a reviewer can understand.
- Order commits by dependency: if change A needs change B, commit B first, then A.
- Keep behavior, supporting refactors, and the tests that prove that behavior in the same commit.
- Do not mix unrelated fixes, generated noise, file-mode changes, or temporary investigation artifacts.
- Before committing, inspect the staged diff and run the narrowest meaningful verification.
- Write an imperative subject that describes the user-visible or architectural outcome.
- Leave every commit buildable and useful on its own; do not depend on a later cleanup commit.
- Preserve unrelated user work. Never amend, squash, reorder, or rewrite existing commits unless asked.
